<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/einstellung-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The tendency for a familiar idea, triggered by features of a position, to stop a player from finding a better solution; in chess it was shown by Bilalić, McLeod and Gobet to work by steering experts' attention towards squares linked to the first idea." .
