<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/forsyth-edwards-notation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A one-line text format that records a complete chess position in six space-separated fields (piece placement, side to move, castling rights, en passant target, halfmove clock and move number); it extends David Forsyth's 1883 position notation and was standardised by Steven J. Edwards in the 1994 PGN specification." .
