<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/jose-raul-capablanca> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Cuban master (1888–1942) and the third official world chess champion, who took the title from Emanuel Lasker in 1921 without losing a game and held it until Alexander Alekhine beat him in 1927; celebrated for clear positional play and endgame technique." .
