<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/mikhail-botvinnik> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Soviet grandmaster (1911–1995) and the sixth world chess champion, who won the vacant title in the 1948 match-tournament and held it three times between 1948 and 1963; regarded as the patriarch of the Soviet chess school for his scientific, methodical approach to preparation and play." .
