<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/monte-carlo-tree-search> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A best-first game-tree search that grows an uneven tree by repeated simulations: each iteration selects a path from the root, expands a new node, estimates its value (by a random playout or a neural network) and backs the result up as an average, so effort concentrates on promising moves." .
