<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/najdorf-variation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The line of the Open Sicilian 1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 a6, in which Black spends a tempo on the quiet ...a6 to keep the choice between ...e5, ...e6 and ...g6 set-ups and prepare queenside expansion; one of the sharpest and most respected defences to 1.e4." .
