<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/queens-gambit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A queen's-pawn opening, 1.d4 d5 2.c4, in which White offers the c-pawn to divert Black's d5-pawn from the centre; because the pawn can usually be regained it is not a true gambit, and Black's main replies are the Slav (2...c6), the Declined (2...e6) and the Accepted (2...dxc4)." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/queens-gambit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Queen's Gambit" .
