<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/rook-endgames> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Endgames in which each side's remaining pieces are rooks (usually one each) plus pawns; they are the most frequent type of endgame in practice, and their outcome depends heavily on the activity of rook and king rather than on material alone." .
