<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/shatranj> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Persian and Arabic form of chess, adopted from the Sasanian game chatrang after the 7th-century Arab conquest of Persia, played with a short-range counsellor and a leaping elephant; it was the game that reached Europe and remained standard there until the late 15th-century rule changes created modern chess." .
