<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/sicilian-defence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A semi-open defence to 1.e4 in which Black answers 1...c5, contesting d4 from the flank and accepting an asymmetrical pawn structure in return for counterplay, typically along the half-open c-file and on the queenside." .
