<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/siegbert-tarrasch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "German master and physician (1862–1934), arguably the world's best tournament player of the 1890s, who won Breslau 1889, Manchester 1890, Dresden 1892, Leipzig 1894 and Vienna 1898, lost the 1908 world championship match to Emanuel Lasker, and as a writer popularised Steinitz's positional principles." .
