<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/slav-defence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Black's reply 2...c6 to the Queen's Gambit (1.d4 d5 2.c4 c6), which supports the d5-pawn without shutting in the queen's bishop and prepares ...dxc4 followed by ...b5; it branches into the Slav Accepted (4...dxc4), the Semi-Slav (4...e6), the Chebanenko (4...a6) and the Exchange Slav (3.cxd5)." .
