<https://github.com/john1hsu/chess-graph/id/template-theory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fernand Gobet and Herbert Simon's 1996 revision of chunking theory, which holds that strong players store frequently met positions as long-term-memory templates: a fixed core of about a dozen pieces plus slots for variable details, plans and moves that can be filled within a fraction of a second." .
